{
  "case_id": "2024-24-394",
  "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "James A. Campbell",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Oklahoma's charter school program relies on private organizations to create more educational options, and it empowers those groups to innovate by giving them broad autonomy over their mission, curriculum, and operations. Fueled by private ingenuity, those schools are thriving as they specialize in diverse subjects like Native American culture and environmental stewardship. But state law categorically bars religious groups and programs, deeming religion to be the wrong kind of diversity. That religious exclusion violates the Free Exercise Clause. This Court has held three times in the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How about if a religious school wanted to change its curriculum to teach only creatism and not evolution? You'd"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: The three cases the Chief Justice referred to -- Trinity Lutheran, Espinoza, and Carson -- involved grants and tax credits. This involves a contract. Is that a relevant constitutional distinction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. And, here, they're not teaching other religions, correct? They're only teaching the Catholic religion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Campbell",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "If the government is picking and choosing a particular religion and not agreeing to allow other religions into the program, then that would be an Establishment Clause violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Campbell",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, one factual point. It's not true that St. Isidore only hires Catholic teachers. It hires teachers that aren't Catholic. That's in the record in Respondent's --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Campbell",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "The state is not running these schools. These schools are run by the privately selected board of directors of each of the schools."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Campbell, you made the point that, historically, states sometimes funded religious schools. Some of the amici on the other side contend, however, that there are historic examples of funding being denied to religious schools and no free exercise claim followed. I wanted to get your thoughts and reactions to that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A student in Oklahoma is free to attend a public school if they choose, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael H. McGinley",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "The Free Exercise Clause bars a state from inviting private parties to participate in an educational funding program while excluding those who exercise their faith. But that is precisely what Oklahoma law does here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0001-0010",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MICHAEL H. McGINLEY ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER IN CASE 24-396"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: You say St. Isidore is not a state actor. What would -- what features would you add to convert St. Isidore into a state actor?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McGinley",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. McGINLEY: So, Justice Thomas, what the Court has said particularly for government entity analysis, is --which is what I take my friend on the other side to really be focused on at this point, is that it requires government creation and control. And so I'd point you to this Court's cases in Lebron, U.S. Olympic Committee, Nebraska, Arkansas. And what Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "McGinley",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "it says is that in all of those cases where the Court found a government entity, there was creation particularly by special legislation where the government literally creates the body. But the Court has also said that's not enough. That's what the U.S. Olympic Committee case says. It says just because the U.S. Olympic Committee was created by special legislation, a charter from Congress, it wasn't controlled by the government because its board was not controlled by the government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: And even absent Smith, I still have to ask whether -- in strict scrutiny, whether the government has a compelling interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: A number of other states, in fact, I think all of them, have the similar kind of program. What should we make of that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: So the federal law is unconstitutional that sets up charter schools and includes as a term the nonsectarian status?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General D. John Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0003-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Charter schools like St. Isidore are not part of the Oklahoma government, and they are not engaged in state action. They are created by private parties applying to public or private sponsors, and they are controlled by privately appointed directors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General, what do we do that two years ago in Peltier versus Charter School, the SG argued the opposite position you're taking today, that charter schools are public schools and state actors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what's the difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice JACKSON",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General Sauer, can I just ask you because, as I understood your response to Justice Sotomayor, you are saying that the portion of the federal law that indicates that to qualify as a charter school you have to be nonsectarian in your programs, you're saying there is a constitutional problem with that or at least there has to be a free exercise exception, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General D. John Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "The entwinement argument, for example, they rely solely on Brentwood Academy, and Brentwood Academy is a case where public officials were 86 percent of the membership of the state athletic association, and they appointed other public officials to control it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Yeah. And one final question. So Justice Kavanaugh explored with you about favoring one religion over another. I'm wondering whether, as a practical matter, that can happen in a situation like this one, where the board can only sponsor five charter schools in a year, for example. I mean, doesn't the board have to determine -- what if we have six applicants or seven from different religions? Would we be in a situation in which the board is picking and choosing among them?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "GENERAL SAUER: The board would have to use religiously neutral criteria. And my understanding is the board says it does that. So it would --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Three considerations distinguish this case from the Trinity Lutheran trilogy and require affirmance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: So, in -- in your -- in the way you look at this case, there is no way that St. Isidore can participate in the charter program and be --and remain private?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: That's right. That's a matter -- that's not me saying it. It's the state saying it. I mean -- and -- and the Oklahoma Supreme Court made this clear. I mean, we've had a lot of statements that St. Isidore is a private institution and not a public school. I -- I mean, what -- what the Oklahoma Supreme Court said was St. Isidore, I'm quoting here, \"came into existence through the charter with the state and will function as a component of the state's public schools system.\" That's at page 30a of the appendix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Oklahoma",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 118,
        "start": 118
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Number one, private schools can open without any state approval. They don't even have to be accredited. Number two, there are no requirements or supervision of curriculum for private schools."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 122,
        "start": 122
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: In terms of the principles, how is it different from a choice program in the -- in the sense that no student is compelled to go to a religious charter school?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0006-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But, here, we have -- we have statement after statement by the attorney general that reeks of hostility toward Islam."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0006-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 130,
        "start": 130
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Absolutely not? That wasn't motivated by the Blaine movement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0006-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 133,
        "start": 133
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "But, at that point, there's a rigorous application process. Curriculum is scrutinized. You have to meet state standards. And then charter schools are regulated extensively, every year evaluated, and they can be closed if they get off the rails because they are public schools."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0006-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 135,
        "start": 135
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Now, with respect -- we've spent a lot of time on is this a state entity or not. But your second theory was that it's a state actor, and that hasn't been discussed that much. How do you deal with West and Rendell-Baker in answering that question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0006-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 137,
        "start": 137
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: If this Court were to rule for Petitioners, what would happen in Oklahoma, in these 40-plus other states with laws of a similar kind that declare charter schools to be public schools? What kind of issues would they have to confront in the future? What do you think the range of choices they would make is likely to be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael H. McGinley",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0006-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 149,
        "start": 149
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. MCGINLEY: A few points. Justice Gorsuch, you asked whether Lebron should control here. The answer is yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0007-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 151,
        "start": 151
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "We completely agree with you, Justice Kavanaugh, that that treats them as second-class citizens. The Free Exercise Clause prohibits that. We ask you to reverse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0007-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 151,
        "start": 151
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "So then the governing question is the same one that this Court confronted in Carson, Espinoza, and Trinity Lutheran: Has the state invited private actors into a government funding program? If so, it cannot categorically exclude the religious."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24-394",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90e3c01ef6654550bb985f24f6a673251334ce0647976c74322dfb3e9bd9e6f6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90e3c01ef665-0007-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 151,
        "start": 151
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
